8,Austronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and Southeast Asia | IIAS,https://www.iias.asia/books/austronesian-soundscapes-performing-arts-oceania-and-southeast-asia,"Ramon P. Santos, Ph.D. UP Center for Ethnomusicology ""The island world of the Pacific and Indian oceans, inhabited by peoples speaking Austronesian languages, has an extremely variegated cultural spectrum. This volume is organised as a musical view on the historical map of the Austronesian expansion, attempting for the first time to see how the performing arts contribute to understanding the interlinkages of this immense cultural area and thus providing a fresh and welcome view on these understudied, yet extremely diverse musical cultures.""",I-wak,Austronesian
9,Austronesian Soundscapes,https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/austronesian-soundscapes/8B714F18DC010F5F8E4997353C4B18BA,"Yet research into the music of Austronesia has hitherto been sparse. Drawing together contemporary cultural studies and musical analysis, Austronesian Soundscapes will fill this research gap, offering a comprehensive analysis of traditional and contemporary Austronesian music and, at the same time, investigating how music reflects the challenges that Austronesian cultures face in this age of globalization.",I-wak,Austronesian
